message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Evaluating Large Language Models for Automated Exploratory Data Analysis and Natural Language-Based Data Querying"
type: generic
authors:
  - family-names: "Malik"
    given-names: "Sidharth"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Applications, Chandigarh University"
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/llm-eda-text-to-sql-evaluation"
abstract: >-
  A survey and comparative evaluation of LLM-based systems for automated
  exploratory data analysis and natural language data querying (Text-to-SQL),
  covering Spider, Spider 2.0, BIRD, LIDA, PandasAI and DAIL-SQL. Proposes a
  5-dimension evaluation framework and argues that LLMs should currently act
  as copilots to human or symbolic analysis rather than standalone analysts.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - text-to-SQL
  - exploratory data analysis
  - benchmarks
  - data analytics
